A||||5||Uaana||Headlight rewire||||1||
Z||000000||Uaana||04-29-2001||09:40 PM||||And yes I searched!<BR>I have the mounts and motors out of an 87+<BR>Does anyone have the rewire instructions to mate it to an older model?<P>And Dont ask me what it is Tina's former Rainbow marvel is a collection of interesting parts. <BR>Still have to figure out the Subwoofer. it's there but not wired.. I'll save that for later lets just get the lights to go up and down first.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||04-30-2001||12:10 AM||||You need to obtain a front wiring harness from an '87-'88 car to do the conversion.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rodmcneill||04-30-2001||12:18 AM||||You also need the module the 87-88's use to control the headlights rather than the earlier relays.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Uaana||04-30-2001||12:34 PM||||Ok got all that. the conversion was done on a 85 SE originally. Now just have to figure out where the new harness mates to the original wiring.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||04-30-2001||01:48 PM||||If you have the harness (complete), module and the headlight motors, remove the old harness. Start at the passenger side and start disconnecting, horn, ground, marker light and the old headlight. Pay attention to routing while removing, the new harness runs in the same places. Then disconnect the same stuff on the drivers side. There is a terminal block to the right and low of the brake booster, it has a bolt keeper just unscrew it and pull the plug. Next you need to push the grommet from the front into the  spare tier well and remove the old harness. Install in reverse, the newer module mounts on the outside of the headlight bucket behind the fender. Access is gained from removing the wheel well liner at the front side to half way around the opening or you may remove it totally.||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||04-30-2001||03:07 PM||||Start at Michigan Fiero Club website.  They have (at least, had) a pretty complete set of instructions for converting to the new system.||||reg||1
